{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "Authorization: every request asks the policy",
  "description": "How a route decides whether the signed-in person may act on a resource, using the embedded Rego policy. Explains the owner-scoping rule behind ENG-108.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/adapters/httpapi/projects.go",
      "line": 559,
      "title": "The check every route makes",
      "description": "`func (a *Server) authorizedSubject` names the action and the resource, asks the policy, and answers 401 when the person is not allowed."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/adapters/httpapi/deployments.go",
      "line": 21,
      "title": "A route names its action",
      "description": "`authorizedSubject` is called with the action project.deploy and the resource owner. Each route picks its own action."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/app/authorization.go",
      "line": 18,
      "title": "The policy, compiled once",
      "description": "`type Policy struct` holds a prepared query over the embedded policy, and is safe for concurrent use."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/app/authorization.go",
      "line": 21,
      "title": "Compiling at startup",
      "description": "`func NewPolicy` compiles the policy when the server starts. A policy that does not compile stops the server before it accepts requests."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/app/authorization.go",
      "line": 35,
      "title": "Asking the policy",
      "description": "`func (p *Policy) Allowed` evaluates the subject, action and resource against the policy."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/app/policy.rego",
      "line": 55,
      "title": "The rule for Deploy",
      "description": "The rule for `project.deploy` allows it only when the subject is the resource owner. That owner check is what keeps another Account out."
    }
  ]
}
